NesSaveRam:0004:npc_records:overworld NPC/rival ship records (SRAM, stride 51; +4=event type, +5=destination port key). A rival's fleet (up to 5 ships) is loaded into combat enemy slots $6C90[5-9] at battle start -- source of the princess-kidnapper finale fleet.
NesSaveRam:0662:entity_table:overworld entity table (party + NPCs), stride 16: +0/+1=x/y (live=Lisbon 32,8), +2/+3=port key f2/f3, +8=facing, +11=EQUIPMENT flags (bit0=Telescope wide-Look, bit1=Sextant position). ch.28 live
NesSaveRam:0664:party_map_x:party position X on the overworld map (party_in_rect, redraw)
NesSaveRam:0665:party_map_y:party position Y on the overworld map
NesSaveRam:066B:gold:player gold/purse (word); capped $EA60=60000. Trade/quest credits, ship/goods debits go here (bank19).
NesSaveRam:0671:sprite_mode_flags:sprite/metasprite mode flags (bit1/bit5 gate place_object_sprite draw paths)
NesSaveRam:07B2:port_econ_records:port economy records, stride 14: +0 economic_worth, +4 industrial_worth, +2/+6 investments, +11 price% source (View->Town shows +11+50 %; live Lisbon 51->101%). ch.28; live EW/IW=800
NesSaveRam:0A9A:mate_roster:active MATE roster: up to 10 slots, 255-terminated, each a byte index into officer records $6542. Fleet width = number of mates (each captains 1 ship). Recruited via event_recruit_sailor; NOT gated by rank/fame directly (gated by player stats*(1+rank/10) vs sailor stats + gold).
NesSaveRam:0B87:os_mode_flags:OS mode-flags byte; mask &4 (bit2)=AUDIO-ENABLED, gates audio_param/reset/playing_gated ($E0C1/$E0D6/$E0EA); (ch.7; bit corrected ch.22)
NesSaveRam:0B89:game_day:in-game day-of-month (draw_day renders mem_6B89+1)
NesSaveRam:0B8A:game_month:in-game month index into name table $BA96 (draw_month)
NesSaveRam:0B8B:game_year_off:in-game year offset; actual year = mem_6B8B + 1500 (draw_year; UW is set in the 1500s)
NesSaveRam:0BAE:hero_record:player hero record (ch.28 live dump): name "Leon Franco" @+0, 5 char-create stats @+$11 (Charisma/Wisdom/Intelligence/Strength/Courage)
NesSaveRam:0BC1:nav_skill:navigation skill (per-port accuracy); Sextant position error = rng if skill<rng(180) (helm_show_position)
NesSaveRam:0C90:ship_records:ship stat records, stride 7: +0 durability,+1 handling,+2 power,+3 arms,+4 crew(word),+6 class/cargo. In COMBAT the array is two fleets: 0-4=yours, 5-9=enemy ($6CB3). Combat caps at 5 ships/side (combat_grid_index).
NesSaveRam:0F70:savings:bank savings deposit (word); capped $2710=10000 (bank19 deposit/withdraw).
NesSaveRam:0F72:fame:FAME / prestige stat (word, cap $C350=50000). NOT "port investment" -- that was my over-narrow mislabel (only saw accrue_port_investment write it). Written by MANY activities: discovery/"Land ho" (bank08 sail_event), trading (bank20), port investment scaled by rank (bank19), outfitting/events (bank21/24). Gain ~= rng(100)+(ship crew+durability)/2 per event. DISPLAYED on the status panel next to gold (bank30 $855B). READ by the court at every quest stage (bank25) = the King-summon/quest gate. Can decay/be spent (bank19 -=rng*5+50).
NesSaveRam:0F74:rank_fame:NOBILITY RANK / title index 0-9 (Page..Duke, Count=7); ptr table bank58 $1C56. Raised ONLY by court-quest completion (bank25, +1/quest, cap 9). Drives ship-bargain discount (10-rank) + court-quest cash reward. Distinct from fame($6F72): fame gates quest AVAILABILITY, rank is the REWARD. Does NOT gate mate recruiting.
NesSaveRam:0FBE:good_price_drift:per-good price-drift array, stride 4 (calc_good_price; floored 100, grows with worth/trade -- NOT the shelf price, which is the goods-table base)
NesSaveRam:1050:player_char_record:main player-character/quest working record $7050-$705F (hottest RAM; ch.6/14)
NesSaveRam:1052:quest_target_port:quest destination port index (compared vs current_port for hook triggers)
NesSaveRam:105F:quest_flags:main quest-progress flag byte (bits gate tavern/court hooks: &1/&2/&8)
NesSaveRam:1062:screen_buffer:main 30x28 nametable tile buffer in RAM; blit_screen_buffer/redraw_* push it to PPU
NesSaveRam:1067:current_port:current port index (indexes port records $67B2 stride14, $AFD8 70-port table stride19, $B50A stride5)
NesSaveRam:1085:dir_delta_x_table:per-direction X step deltas (step_entity indexes by facing)
NesSaveRam:1087:dir_delta_y_table:per-direction Y step deltas (step_entity indexes by facing)
